{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775367566,"nonce":"mPZ8rD4Sr6TJkmdnJuhyCNMO+dU=","title":"Manual `nightshift start` with short ID prefix creates duplicate session when one already exists under full ID.","message":"`nightshift start 64dd713` creates a new session with `issue_id: 64dd713` even though a session for the same issue already exists at `64dd71361d31` with the full issue ID. Two sessions now compete for the same issue, with different branches and worktrees.\n\n\n`launch.py` creates sessions using whatever issue ID string was passed on the command line. It doesn't normalize to the full hash or check for existing sessions with a matching prefix.\n\nThe auto-start code in `session_monitor.py` (line 469-475) builds `existing_issue_ids` from `state.get(\"issue_id\")` and checks `issue.id in existing_issue_ids` — but this is exact string match. `\"64dd713\" != \"64dd71361d31...\"`.\n\n\n```\n64dd713        working                        0    0  Parser adds Results todo and not-yet...\n64dd71361d31   suspended:too-complex          0    0  Parser adds Results todo and not-yet...\n```\n\nSession `64dd71361d31` started by auto-start (full ID). Session `64dd713` started manually 5 hours later (short prefix). Both for the same issue.\n\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_start_rejects_duplicate_session_by_prefix\n  Assert: starting with short ID when full-ID session exists fails with error message\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_start_rejects_duplicate_session_by_full_id\n  Assert: starting with full ID when short-ID session exists fails with error message\n- tests/watcher/test_session_monitor.py::test_auto_start_skips_prefix_match\n  Assert: auto-start skips issue when existing session matches by prefix\n\n- host/launch.py (modify — check for existing sessions with matching prefix before creating)\n- host/watcher/session_monitor.py (modify — use prefix matching for existing_issue_ids check)\n\n1. In `launch.py`, before creating worktree/session:\n   - Scan `.nightshift/sessions/*/state.json` for any `issue_id` that starts with the given ID or vice versa\n   - If found, print error and exit: \"Session already exists: \u003cexisting_sid\u003e\"\n2. In `session_monitor.py` auto-start, change `existing_issue_ids` check to use prefix matching:\n   - `any(issue.id.startswith(eid) or eid.startswith(issue.id) for eid in existing_issue_ids)`\n\nREQ: REQ-001 (session lifecycle)","files":null}]}